# Corpus runs held out of version control pending a licence decision.
#
# Two categories, both on disk and usable locally, neither committed:
#
#  1. Unidentified licence — GitHub reports NOASSERTION for a LICENSE file it
#     cannot classify, which is not the same as having no licence. The harvester
#     skips these by default; they are here only because --allow-unlicensed was
#     passed for local measurement.
#
#  2. Copyleft — GPL/LGPL/AGPL. crux itself is Apache-2.0, and committing
#     copyleft-derived content into it is a decision for a human, not a default.
#     The stored payload is failure messages and stack traces, which is arguably
#     factual CI output rather than licensed expression, but "arguably" is not a
#     basis for putting it in git history.
#
# Force-add an individual run to override: git add -f corpus/runs/<dir>
